### Versioning and Releasing

```bash
# Dry run to see what will change
poe drybump patch

# Bump the version, commit, tag and push
poe bump patch  # or minor, or major

# Publish the new version to PyPI
gh release create vX.Y.Z --generate-notes
```

`poe bump` refuses to run if the current version was never published to PyPI
(set `BUMP_ALLOW_UNRELEASED=1` to override). In a new project, publish the initial
version with `gh release create v{{ initial_version }} --generate-notes` before the first bump.

Creating a GitHub Release runs `.github/workflows/publish.yml`, which checks the tag,
runs the tests, builds, and uploads to PyPI using trusted publishing. One-time setup:

1. On PyPI, add a trusted publisher (a "pending publisher" if the project doesn't exist yet):
   owner `{{ github_user }}`, repository `{{ project_slug }}`, workflow `publish.yml`, environment `pypi`.
2. On GitHub, create an environment named `pypi` in the repo settings.
